From 0ed7d3b7bcac1ea08e4687cf7bafce9e8abb22ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 21:47:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rc/www: guard nvram reads in generated scripts, diag store
 section, kp v6 skip, WGC rule flag

- rc/reaper_nv.h: REAPER_NV_HELPER - `_nv` = nvram get with a 5 s ceiling
  (background + 20 ms poll, SIGKILL + one `reaper-nv` syslog line on hang).
  Emitted after the shebang of every generated Warden script (apply/fold/
  stats/update) and rwatch.sh; all $(nvram get x) in those scripts -> $(_nv x).
  Metal-tested on busybox ash: 28 ms/call normal, hung reader killed at 5 s,
  empty value, no temp leftovers.
- rc/rwatch.c: per-tick reaper for any `nvram` process older than 120 s
  (libnvram netlink wait-forever), logged with cmdline + age.
  Field case 2026-08-21 v2.6.0: fold.sh's `nvram get rwarden_stats_save`
  asleep in __skb_wait_for_more_packets for 5 h with wlcsm_bindfix=1,
  holding ctr.lock.
- others/reaper_diag: section 17 resolves the durable store like rwatch.sh
  (reaper_store/jffs/usb) and reports the syslog mirror path/size/span,
  history logs and the incident dir; /jffs/rwatch absence = healthy.
- rc/rwarden.c: skip the ipdeny v6 zone fetch for countries that publish
  none (kp) instead of logging "geo v6 fetch FAILED" nightly.
- www/Reaper_VPNRouting.asp: WGC1-5 targets render as an amber dashed chip
  with RVR_53 ("not supported yet - rule inactive"); 25 dicts lockstep.
